{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"70e2ecda-8cb8-4840-9081-02446080483a","title":"Derivative as slope at a point"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"70e2ecda-8cb8-4840-9081-02446080483a","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Slope measures rise divided by run. On a curve, the slope can change from point to point.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"slope","region":"A1","latex":"\\text{slope}=\\frac{\\text{rise}}{\\text{run}}"},{"op":"axes","id":"axes","region":"right","x":{"min":0,"max":2,"label":"x"},"y":{"min":0,"max":4,"label":"y"}},{"op":"curve","id":"parabola","axes_id":"axes","expr":"x^2","domain":[0,2]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.warning","request_id":"70e2ecda-8cb8-4840-9081-02446080483a","code":"step_repaired","step_hint":"s2"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"70e2ecda-8cb8-4840-9081-02446080483a","step":{"id":"s2","script":"For y equals x squared, compare x equals one with a nearby point. The secant slope measures change across that interval.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"secant_work","anchor":{"el":"slope","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\frac{(1+h)^2-1}{h}=2+h\\quad(h\\neq0)"},{"op":"curve","id":"secant","axes_id":"axes","expr":"2.5*x-1.5","domain":[0.6,2]}],"checkpoint":{"question":"As h approaches zero, what value does the secant slope 2 + h approach?","expected_gist":"It approaches 2."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"70e2ecda-8cb8-4840-9081-02446080483a","step":{"id":"s3","script":"As the interval shrinks to zero, the secant approaches the tangent. Its slope is the derivative at x equals one.","ops":[{"op":"line","id":"tangent","construct":{"kind":"tangent_at","curve":"parabola","x":1,"length":0.55},"stroke":"solid","label":"tangent"},{"op":"equation","id":"limit","anchor":{"el":"secant_work","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"f'(1)=\\lim_{h\\to0}(2+h)=2"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"70e2ecda-8cb8-4840-9081-02446080483a","step":{"id":"s4","script":"So near x equals one, a small horizontal change produces approximately twice as much vertical change. The tangent captures this local behavior.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"local","anchor":{"el":"limit","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\Delta y\\approx2\\,\\Delta x"},{"op":"equation","id":"tangent_eq","anchor":{"el":"local","side":"below","gap":0.06},"latex":"\\text{Tangent: }y-1=2(x-1)"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.done","request_id":"70e2ecda-8cb8-4840-9081-02446080483a","accepted_steps":4,"repairs":1,"dropped_steps":0,"sanitized_steps":0,"sanitized_fields":0}
